  "description": "Issue #6 mechanics-hook RELEASE runtime proof on a starter-foundation profile ROM (EXPANSION_MECHANICS_HOOKS=1 EXPANSION_MECHANICS_SAMPLE=1), reached by the SAME ordinary clean-boot Normal-difficulty route as starter-danger-overlay-modern-release.json -- no save fixture, no debug launcher, no debug tools: the shared title/save-menu A/START cadence, New Game, one DOWN to NORMAL (difficultyConfigByte, PlaySt.config.controller at gPlaySt+0x42, reads 0x20 with PLAY_FLAG_HARD clear), the first empty slot, then eleven START presses on the engine's own skip path (src/event.c). The Prologue's opening event contains a REAL scripted bout in which Seth fights a Grado soldier, so ComputeBattleUnitStats() genuinely runs: Seth (gUnitArrayBlue[0]) is 30/30 before it and 13/30 after, damage the engine itself resolved. Across that bout the semantic scalar counters show the seam behaved exactly as specified -- the sample registered once through the public API (registerOkCount=1) with no rejected registration (registerErrCount=0, lastResult=0 OK), the seam applied once per combatant (applyCount=2), each apply iterated exactly the one registered mechanic (lastAppliedCount=1), the net battleDefense delta of the last apply was the sample's bounded +1 (lastDefenseDelta=1), and the full-HP guard fired for both full-HP combatants (sampleTriggerCount=2). The counters are then shown stable once the ordinary Prologue battle map is live and interactive (chapterIndex CHAPTER_L_PROLOGUE 0x00, faction FACTION_BLUE 0x00, chapterTurnNumber 1, mapSize 15x10, boss 23/23). Semantic scalars only -- never a pointer, never a framebuffer hash.",
